WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.451
The first hour of a

2
00:00:01.451 --> 00:00:03.232
sitting is Question Hour.

3
00:00:03.232 --> 00:00:04.523
What comes right after it

4
00:00:04.523 --> 00:00:05.964
isn't in any rule.

5
00:00:06.284 --> 00:00:08.620
Starred questions get oral answers,

6
00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:10.859
and members can ask follow-ups.

7
00:00:10.859 --> 00:00:12.479
Unstarred ones are answered in

8
00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:14.565
writing. Short notice questions deal

9
00:00:14.565 --> 00:00:16.217
with urgent matters.

10
00:00:16.552 --> 00:00:18.460
Zero Hour began as a

11
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:21.276
practice in the early 1960s.

12
00:00:21.276 --> 00:00:23.378
Members raise urgent issues without

13
00:00:23.378 --> 00:00:24.302
prior notice.

14
00:00:24.302 --> 00:00:26.479
It's an Indian innovation.

15
00:00:26.835 --> 00:00:27.626
In GS2,

16
00:00:27.626 --> 00:00:29.114
use them as tools of

17
00:00:29.114 --> 00:00:31.497
accountability. And note how often

18
00:00:31.497 --> 00:00:33.538
disruptions cut them short.

19
00:00:34.214 --> 00:00:35.391
Your turn.

20
00:00:35.391 --> 00:00:37.808
Which one allows supplementaries?
